    {
      "id": "el112",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1700113407,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1989259376,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "type": "text",
      "x": 300,
      "y": 2280,
      "width": 304.2,
      "height": 48.75,
      "text": "S3 is deliberately LAST.\nthe bytes outlive the row for 30 days\nso an accidental delete is recoverable.",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "S3 is deliberately LAST.\nthe bytes outlive the row for 30 days\nso an accidental delete is recoverable.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "el113",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#e7f5ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3
      },
      "seed": 1723943247,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 364725392,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 2060,
      "y": 170,
      "width": 880,
      "height": 958.5
    },
    {
      "id": "el114",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 682281554,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 730160160,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2080,
      "y": 188,
      "width": 203.32,
      "height": 21.25,
      "text": "FETCH  \u2014  the decisions",
      "fontSize": 17,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "FETCH  \u2014  the decisions",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "el115",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 545625653,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 118321418,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2080,
      "y": 223,
      "width": 530.4,
      "height": 877.5,
      "text": "WHERE EACH PIECE COMES FROM\n\nmetadata, status, title, mime, page_count  ->  Postgres, always\nbody,  <= 256 KB                           ->  the row, inlined\nbody,  >  256 KB                           ->  a LINK, never inlined\n\n    GET /documents/{id}         metadata + status + links\n    GET /documents/{id}/text    302 -> presigned S3 /text\n    GET /documents/{id}/raw     302 -> presigned S3 /raw\n\n\nTHERE IS NO ?include=text\n\nit would only ever have been needed for documents over 256 KB  \u2014\nexactly the ones too big to inline.  a 20 MB PDF extracts to ~2 MB\nof text: buffered in memory, JSON-escaped to ~2.4 MB, and\nimpossible to stream out of a JSON field.\n\nthe redirect costs the service nothing and works the same at 20 KB\nor 200 MB.  one endpoint shape, no size logic.\n\n\nWHY POSTGRES AND NOT ELASTICSEARCH\n\nPostgres is the source of truth and always fresh.  a document still\nin PENDING is fetchable immediately  \u2014  in Elasticsearch it does\nnot exist until status = LIVE.  this is the endpoint a client polls\nafter a 202, so it has to answer during PENDING.\n\n\nWHY THE PRIMARY, NOT A REPLICA\n\n    t+0     POST  ->  row written to the primary, 202 returned\n    t+20ms  GET   ->  hits a replica that has not caught up\n                  ->  404 on a document that plainly exists\n\nsearch reads replicas freely.  this endpoint cannot  \u2014  it is the\none clients hit immediately after writing.  a primary-key lookup,\nmostly served by Redis, so the primary can take it.\n\n\n404, NEVER 403\n\n    SELECT ... WHERE tenant_id = $1 AND id = $2\n\nzero rows on a wrong-tenant lookup, so it 404s naturally.  a 403\nwould confirm the document exists  \u2014  an id enumeration leak.\n\n\nTHE CACHE:   d:{tenant}:{doc_id}   TTL 300 s\n\nthe Indexer DELETEs that exact key when status changes.  a single\nDEL works because you know the key; the query cache has thousands\nof unknown keys, which is why it uses a version counter instead.",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "WHERE EACH PIECE COMES FROM\n\nmetadata, status, title, mime, page_count  ->  Postgres, always\nbody,  <= 256 KB                           ->  the row, inlined\nbody,  >  256 KB                           ->  a LINK, never inlined\n\n    GET /documents/{id}         metadata + status + links\n    GET /documents/{id}/text    302 -> presigned S3 /text\n    GET /documents/{id}/raw     302 -> presigned S3 /raw\n\n\nTHERE IS NO ?include=text\n\nit would only ever have been needed for documents over 256 KB  \u2014\nexactly the ones too big to inline.  a 20 MB PDF extracts to ~2 MB\nof text: buffered in memory, JSON-escaped to ~2.4 MB, and\nimpossible to stream out of a JSON field.\n\nthe redirect costs the service nothing and works the same at 20 KB\nor 200 MB.  one endpoint shape, no size logic.\n\n\nWHY POSTGRES AND NOT ELASTICSEARCH\n\nPostgres is the source of truth and always fresh.  a document still\nin PENDING is fetchable immediately  \u2014  in Elasticsearch it does\nnot exist until status = LIVE.  this is the endpoint a client polls\nafter a 202, so it has to answer during PENDING.\n\n\nWHY THE PRIMARY, NOT A REPLICA\n\n    t+0     POST  ->  row written to the primary, 202 returned\n    t+20ms  GET   ->  hits a replica that has not caught up\n                  ->  404 on a document that plainly exists\n\nsearch reads replicas freely.  this endpoint cannot  \u2014  it is the\none clients hit immediately after writing.  a primary-key lookup,\nmostly served by Redis, so the primary can take it.\n\n\n404, NEVER 403\n\n    SELECT ... WHERE tenant_id = $1 AND id = $2\n\nzero rows on a wrong-tenant lookup, so it 404s naturally.  a 403\nwould confirm the document exists  \u2014  an id enumeration leak.\n\n\nTHE CACHE:   d:{tenant}:{doc_id}   TTL 300 s\n\nthe Indexer DELETEs that exact key when status changes.  a single\nDEL works because you know the key; the query cache has thousands\nof unknown keys, which is why it uses a version counter instead.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "el116",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffe3e3",
