      "width": 880,
      "height": 633.5
    },
    {
      "id": "el117",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 627813882,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 2037347502,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2080,
      "y": 1196.5,
      "width": 212.16,
      "height": 21.25,
      "text": "DELETE  \u2014  the decisions",
      "fontSize": 17,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "DELETE  \u2014  the decisions",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "el118",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1504988819,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 669638768,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2080,
      "y": 1231.5,
      "width": 522.6,
      "height": 552.5,
      "text": "WHY SOFT DELETE\n\n    UPDATE status = 'DELETED'      not  DELETE FROM\n\nthe row is what tells the async cleanup what to clean.  delete it\noutright and nothing downstream knows the document existed.  it\nalso buys an undelete window and keeps the audit trail.\n\n\nTHE WINDOW YOU MUST DECLARE\n\n204 returns before Elasticsearch has dropped the document, so for\n~1-2 s a deleted document is still findable.  same eventual\nconsistency as indexing, for the same reason.\n\nbut if step 8 fails into the DLQ it stays findable FOREVER.  that\nis a correctness bug, not lag  \u2014  alert on that queue specifically,\nand run a nightly job reconciling DELETED rows against the index.\n\n\nS3 COMES LAST, ON PURPOSE\n\n/raw and /text survive the undelete window (30 days), then the\nretention job purges them.\n\na GDPR erasure request skips the window entirely: purge now, and\nverify the Elasticsearch delete landed.  \"we soft-deleted it\" is\nnot erasure.\n\n\nDELETING MID-UPLOAD\n\nstatus = AWAITING_UPLOAD also needs AbortMultipartUpload, or the\nuploaded parts sit in S3 billed and invisible in the object list.",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "WHY SOFT DELETE\n\n    UPDATE status = 'DELETED'      not  DELETE FROM\n\nthe row is what tells the async cleanup what to clean.  delete it\noutright and nothing downstream knows the document existed.  it\nalso buys an undelete window and keeps the audit trail.\n\n\nTHE WINDOW YOU MUST DECLARE\n\n204 returns before Elasticsearch has dropped the document, so for\n~1-2 s a deleted document is still findable.  same eventual\nconsistency as indexing, for the same reason.\n\nbut if step 8 fails into the DLQ it stays findable FOREVER.  that\nis a correctness bug, not lag  \u2014  alert on that queue specifically,\nand run a nightly job reconciling DELETED rows against the index.\n\n\nS3 COMES LAST, ON PURPOSE\n\n/raw and /text survive the undelete window (30 days), then the\nretention job purges them.\n\na GDPR erasure request skips the window entirely: purge now, and\nverify the Elasticsearch delete landed.  \"we soft-deleted it\" is\nnot erasure.\n\n\nDELETING MID-UPLOAD\n\nstatus = AWAITING_UPLOAD also needs AbortMultipartUpload, or the\nuploaded parts sit in S3 billed and invisible in the object list.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "el119",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 562571391,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 91898035,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "type": "text",
      "x": 80,
      "y": 2480,
      "width": 309.40000000000003,
      "height": 21.25,
      "text": "THE SHAPE ALL THREE ENDPOINTS SHARE",
      "fontSize": 17,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "THE SHAPE ALL THREE ENDPOINTS SHARE",
