      "locked": false,
      "type": "text",
      "x": 80,
      "y": 2512,
      "width": 562.8,
      "height": 157.5,
      "text": "1  the tenant filter lives in the WHERE clause, so isolation is not\n   something a handler can forget to apply\n2  Postgres answers, Elasticsearch is never consulted  \u2014  these are\n   point lookups by primary key, not searches\n3  bytes NEVER pass through the service.  metadata endpoints return\n   links, byte endpoints return a 302.  size stops mattering.\n4  the write is synchronous and small, the cleanup is asynchronous\n   and rides the SAME Debezium pipeline that indexing uses\n5  nothing is ever hard-deleted on the request path",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1  the tenant filter lives in the WHERE clause, so isolation is not\n   something a handler can forget to apply\n2  Postgres answers, Elasticsearch is never consulted  \u2014  these are\n   point lookups by primary key, not searches\n3  bytes NEVER pass through the service.  metadata endpoints return\n   links, byte endpoints return a 302.  size stops mattering.\n4  the write is synchronous and small, the cleanup is asynchronous\n   and rides the SAME Debezium pipeline that indexing uses\n5  nothing is ever hard-deleted on the request path",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
